Requirements: 21   with obligations: 20   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Requirement decomposition must preserve two distinctions when it reads a task
    file: an acceptance criterion demanding a test, against the behaviour that test is
    about; and a scope exclusion, against work the change must do.
    -> preserve-test-vs-behaviour-distinction  [functional/explicit]
       Preserve the distinction between an acceptance criterion that demands a test and
       the behaviour that test is about.
    -> preserve-scope-exclusion-distinction  [functional/explicit]
       Preserve the distinction between a scope exclusion and the work the change must
       do.

[constraint-01] An acceptance criterion that demands a test yields an obligation whose
    demand is the test, not the behaviour the test is about.
    -> acceptance-criterion-yields-test-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       Map an acceptance criterion that demands a test to an obligation whose demand is
       the test rather than the behavior under test.

[constraint-02] An obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test
    of that behaviour are never recognised as stating the same requirement.
    -> behavior-and-test-distinct-requirements  [invariant/explicit]
       Keep an obligation demanding a behaviour distinct from an obligation demanding a
       test of that behaviour when recognizing requirements.

[constraint-03] A sentence of a given shape yields the same kind of obligation
    regardless of which task file it appears in.
    -> sentence-shape-consistent-obligation-kind  [invariant/explicit]
       A sentence of a given shape yields the same kind of obligation in every task
       file.

[constraint-04] Sibling bullets under one scope exclusions heading receive the same
    disposition as each other.
    -> sibling-bullets-same-disposition  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves completion-04)
       Preserve the rule that sibling bullets worded alike under one scope exclusions
       heading receive the same disposition as each other.

[constraint-05] A requirement disposed of without an obligation carries a reason that
    does not itself state a property the change must preserve.
    -> reason-no-preserved-property  [docs_config/explicit]   (also serves completion-05)
       Produce a reason for no-obligation dispositions that states no property the
       change must preserve.

[constraint-06] No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test
    that an excluded thing did not happen.
    -> no-obligation-for-excluded-thing-not-happened-test-evidence  [invariant/explicit]
       No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test that an
       excluded thing did not happen.

[constraint-07] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-06)
       Preserve byte-identical review state across two runs over byte-identical task
       text.

[constraint-08] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-issue-no-live-model-calls  [invariant/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

[exclusion-01] Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all, which is #148.
    -> test-evidence-question-out-of-scope  [compatibility/explicit]
       Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all is out of scope for this change.

[exclusion-02] Assigning obligation types, which is #205.
    -> obligation-types-assignment-out-of-scope  [compatibility/explicit]
       Assigning obligation types is out of scope for this change.

[exclusion-03] Which open questions are raised, and what they cite, which is #206.
    -> open-questions-and-citations  [human_review/explicit]
       Raise open questions when the task text is materially underspecified, and include
       what each question cites.

[exclusion-04] How finely a single requirement is split into obligations, which is #117.
    -> requirement-splitting-granularity  [functional/explicit]
       Split a single requirement into obligations at the level of distinct computations
       or behaviors, keeping cohesive behaviors whole.

[exclusion-05] Whether obligation identifiers are stable across task-file edits, which
    is #231.
    -> stable-obligation-identifiers  [invariant/explicit]
       Keep obligation identifiers stable across edits to the task file.

[exclusion-06] Measuring how accurate decomposition is, which is #211.
    -> decomposition-accuracy-measurement  [human_review/explicit]
       Measure how accurate the decomposition is.

[completion-01] Implementation
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       A standalone section marker with no checkable requirement.

